 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "It is necessary / I have to",
     "texto": [
      "To say «one has to» or «I have to», **нужно** or **надо** + dative + infinitive is used: **Мне нужно идти** (I have to go), **Тебе надо отдохнуть** (you have to rest).",
      "In this construction, **нужно** and **надо** express necessity and are followed by the infinitive.",
      "**Должен / должна / должны** + infinitive expresses a personal obligation and agrees in gender and number with the subject in the nominative: **Я должен идти** (said by a man), **Я должна идти** (said by a woman), **Мы должны идти** (plural).",
      "**Придётся** + infinitive expresses a necessity that is imposed: **Мне придётся идти** (I'll have to go)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Being able to do something",
     "texto": [
      "**Мочь** means «can» in the sense of having ability or possibility and is conjugated: **я могу, ты можешь, он/она может, мы можем, вы можете, они могут**. It is followed by an infinitive: **Я могу прийти** (I can come). **Можно** + infinitive expresses permission or general possibility; **нельзя** expresses that something is not allowed."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Allowed / not allowed",
     "texto": [
      "**Можно** + infinitive is used to ask for permission: **Можно войти?** (may I come in?). **Нельзя** + infinitive expresses prohibition: **Здесь нельзя курить** (smoking is forbidden here).",
      "The perfective verbs **отдохнуть** and **помочь** present the action as a bounded whole; their imperfective partners **отдыхать** and **помогать** focus on the process or repetition. **Мне нельзя опоздать** means I must not be late."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
